turns.assistantResponse:
Fixed the CI failure.

What was wrong:
- `app.js` started the Express server immediately when the module was imported.
- That breaks CI/test environments because requiring the app binds port `3000` as a side effect.

What I changed:
- Wrapped `app.listen(...)` in:

```js
if (require.main === module) {
  app.listen(3000, () => {
    console.log('Server running on port 3000');
  });
}
```

- This preserves normal behavior when running `node app.js`, but allows tests/CI to safely import `app.js`.

I also added the missing `ci-check.sh` in this workspace so the requested command can run locally, and verified:

```bash
bash ci-check.sh
```

now passes.

